{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. I did not request implementation source. Obligations are mapped to tests below.\n\n**Combine every applicable contribution.**\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` asserts the bundle for a requirement subject.\n  - It includes the subject declaration, cited requirements, referenced examples, `{test}` items and terms.\n  - It excludes `{impl}` items and distant requirements.\n  - It does not carry forward earlier evidence inputs or judgments.\n- `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` covers which edges contribute. It checks the cite, test and impl directions and the example and parent cases.\n- `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` cover `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors. The first asserts the exact input list. The second asserts that only the selected node reaches the prompt.\n- `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` covers reference-owning outline nodes and `{fixme}` metadata.\n- `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` covers the exclusion rules.\n- The `src/authoring/mod.rs` tests `fn[citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations]`, `fn[book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance]` and `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` cover the citation, book-commentary and site subject kinds.\n\n**Deduplicate identical selections.**\n- `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` has duplicate cites, a term shared by two requirements, and a repeated built-in. It asserts each appears exactly once and that the total is 5.\n- `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` names the same file in `:impl:` and `:test:`. It asserts that only one input results.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` covers deduplication in recorded evidence.\n\n**Report unresolvable inputs before inference.**\n- `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` covers a missing file, a missing node, and an ignored file. It asserts the error text and path.\n- `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` covers an ignored declaration file.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request]` ignores the declaration file. It asserts a nonzero exit, that stderr names the path, that the model endpoint was never contacted, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n- `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` shows that stale inputs recorded in earlier evidence are not mandatory inputs.\n\n**Supply the complete set in the initial request.**\n- The Ollama CLI test asserts that the initial prompt contains the requirement, the definition text and `fn ready_test()`. It also asserts that the prepared inputs equal the delivered inputs.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read]` also checks the initial prompt contents.\n- The citation test asserts that the prompt contains the item, the requirement and the built-in text.\n\n**Visibility under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`.**\n- `fn[mandatory_anchors_respect_git_metadata_and_nested_ignore_exceptions]` covers `.git` metadata, a nested ignore file, and the `!keep.rs` exception. It asserts both the denial and the permitted case.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_abort_preparation]` and `fn[outside_test_anchors_stay_outside_the_project_with_an_allow_rule]` cover files outside the project. The second covers both absolute and relative anchors.\n- `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` covers ignored directories and symlink aliases.\n- `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` covers untracked files being available.\n\n**Denied selections abort under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.** This is a cited requirement, so I did not reassess it. The tests above check the abort, the `PermissionDenied` kind and the path in the error.\n\nThe clause that a contributing requirement must cite this requirement is a rule for other requirements' text. It is not behaviour of the harness. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "378c9484242a7605f9e49a951f8956fe0a3a3cedf2b63ccf5aa285ff444949c5",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} mandatory_inputs",
        "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining",
        "the contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and",
        "its inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and",
        "define which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every",
        "applicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report",
        "unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied",
        "in the initial model request.",
        "A file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort",
        "under {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} local_provider",
        "Source inspection uses the project directory and respects `.gitignore`,",
        "including nested ignore files and their exceptions. Untracked files are",
        "available unless ignored. The same scope applies to listing, reading,",
        "outlining, text search, and structural search, including requests naming a",
        "file or subdirectory directly.",
        "",
        "Files outside the project directory and Git metadata are excluded. A direct",
        "read of an excluded file returns an error.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} read_denial.mandatory",
        "When source-access policy denies a mandatory input, the assessment MUST abort",
        "before any model request and report the denied path and reason to its caller. The aborted assessment MUST NOT write evidence or emit evidence JSON, and",
        "its usage record MUST identify the failure. In a batch, other assessments MUST",
        "continue, including queued assessments, and their successful writes MUST be",
        "retained; the command MUST return a nonzero exit status after the batch",
        "finishes.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
